    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nThe frai CLI's `gate` command was not properly forwarding the `--ci` flag to the frai-gate CLI. The issue was in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (line 753), where the code only passed the captured positional arguments, not the full command-line arguments including flags.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified the gate command handler to pass all raw arguments from `process.argv` after the 'gate' keyword, which includes both positional arguments and flags like `--ci`. This ensures that all options are correctly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Verification:**\n- \u2705 Built the frai-cli package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory\n- \u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` files are now created correctly",
